From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the cache-line size assumption check on riscv64

Arch_ValidateAssumptions() runs on every load of libusd_arch and compares
ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE (pxr/base/arch/align.h: 128 on Apple ARM, 64 everywhere
else) with Arch_ObtainCacheLineSize(), i.e. sysconf(_SC_LEVEL1_DCACHE_LINESIZE)
on Linux. On a mismatch it prints a four-line " ArchWarn: ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE
!= Arch_ObtainCacheLineSize()" block straight to stderr with fprintf
(arch/error.cpp), below the Tf diagnostics layer, so no environment setting or
diagnostic delegate can silence it.

On riscv64 the comparison has nothing to check. The ISA defines no cache-line
size; it varies between implementations. glibc's riscv sysconf reads it from
the AT_L1D_CACHEGEOMETRY auxv entry, which the kernel fills from the
firmware's devicetree/ACPI cache description and sets to 0 when there is none
(arch/riscv/kernel/cacheinfo.c). Whatever value align.h picks for riscv64 is
therefore "wrong" on some machines, and the warning fires on every process
that imports pxr on those machines: every user of the wheel sees it, and
every test that checks a subprocess's stderr exactly fails because of it
(usd-exchange's testDiagnostics.py assertOutputStreams() and
testSettings.py's empty-stderr assertion).

Keep ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE at its 64 default (it only sizes padding and
alignment, so a mismatch costs performance, never correctness) and skip the
comparison when ARCH_CPU_RISCV is defined (added by the previous patch). The
other checks in Arch_ValidateAssumptions(), including the big-endian
ARCH_ERROR, are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; belongs with the riscv64 arch support of the previous patch in a pull request against PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD]
---
 pxr/base/arch/assumptions.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pxr/base/arch/assumptions.cpp b/pxr/base/arch/assumptions.cpp
index 1029b32..f0c63df 100644
--- a/pxr/base/arch/assumptions.cpp
+++ b/pxr/base/arch/assumptions.cpp
@@ -135,10 +135,18 @@ Arch_ValidateAssumptions()
     /*
      * Make sure that the ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE constant is set as expected
      * on the current hardware architecture.
+     *
+     * RISC-V has no architectural cache-line size: it varies between
+     * implementations, and Linux reports whatever the firmware describes
+     * (0 when it describes none), so there is no constant to validate.
      */ 
+#if !defined(ARCH_CPU_RISCV)
     if (ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE != cacheLineSize) {
         ARCH_WARNING("ARCH_CACHE_LINE_SIZE != Arch_ObtainCacheLineSize()");
     }
+#else
+    (void)cacheLineSize;
+#endif
 
     /*
      * Make sure that the machine is little-endian.  We do not support
